# Chrome 153's property grammars for CSS.supports() and @supports (lb-css
# supports_value.rs). `name = syntax` per property Chrome knows (and only those),
# `<name> = syntax` per type, `<'name'> = syntax` for a property Chrome does not
# know that a grammar refers to. CSS value definition syntax, plus: `a ^^ b`
# (Blink's greedy `||`: parts in order, longest match, no backtracking),
# `<custom-ident ~none ~auto>` (excluded keywords), `<string [4,4]>` (length).
# Built into supports_value.rs, not here: <length> <percentage>
# <length-percentage> <number> <integer> <angle> <angle-percentage> <time>
# <time-percentage> <frequency> <resolution> <flex> <zero> <dimension> <string>
# <url> <ident> <custom-ident> <dashed-ident> <custom-property-name> <hex-color>
# <named-color> <declaration-value> <any-value> <family-name> <path-data>
# <calc-size()> <length-lit> (no math functions) <length-unit> (no unitless 0)
# <number-eval> (ranges bound math functions too), math functions in numeric
# types. Seeded from the specs (@webref/css, MIT), edited to match Chrome 153's
# answers on lb-page/tests/css_supports/corpus.jsonl.
